s place:**  \n     \\(6 + 2 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 9\\)  \n     Write down **9**.\n\n   - **Hundreds place:**  \n     \\(8 + 8 = 16\\)  \n     Write down **6** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n   - **Thousands place:**  \n     \\(6 + 2 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 9\\)  \n     Write down **9**.\n\n   - **Ten-thousands place:**  \n     \\(4 + 8 = 12\\)  \n     Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the hundred-thousands place.\n\n   - **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n     \\(7 + 9 + 1\\) (carried over) \\(= 17\\)  \n     Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n   - **Millions place:**  \n     There's only the carried-over **1**.  \n     Write down **1**.\n\n3. **Combine all the digits to get the final sum:**\n\n   \\[\n   1,\\!729,\\!697\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1,\\!729,\\!697}\\)..Therefore, the answer is"]]
